    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d154">

                <pb facs="0304" n="1762" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p2/pg1762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">794A.022/7–2351: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Republic of China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Rankin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Taipei</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-07-23T16:00:00+09:00">July 23, 1951—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>105. During private discussion of US-Australia-Canberra [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >New Zealand</hi>] tripartite pact<anchor n="1" xml:id="d154-f1"/> with
                        FonMin<anchor n="2" xml:id="d154-f2"/>
                    today he asked me whether Dept had any plans for including Chi Govt and more
                    specifically Formosa in similar arrangement. He pointed out Phil demand for
                    defense pact with US<anchor n="3" xml:id="d154-f3"/> might bring up related
                    problems affecting Formosa including Seventh Fleet’s mission.</p>
                <p>Replied I assumed Dept had considered above questions in relation Formosa but
                    view polit problems involved it premature take position in matter. I expressed
                    hope tripartite pact was only first step in more comprehensive security
                    arrangements in Pacific and suggested Chi Govt give matter continuing study to
                    determine how it might fit into collective security system as it develops in
                        FE.</p>
                <p>
                    FonMin requested I put question in para one
                    to Dept in any case.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rankin</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d154-f1" n="1" xml:id="d154-f1-content">
                <p>For documentation concerning the security treaty between Australia, New Zealand,
                    and the United States, signed at San Francisco on September 1, 1951, see <ref
                        target="frus1951v06p1#pg_132">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, Part
                        1, pp. 132</ref> ff. For the text of the treaty, see 3 UST (pt. 3) 3420.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f2" n="2" xml:id="d154-f2-content">
                <p>George Kung-Chao Yen, Minister of Foreign Affairs, Republic of China.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d154-f3" n="3" xml:id="d154-f3-content">
                <p>For documentation regarding the mutual defense treaty between the Philippines and
                    the United States, signed at Washington on August 30, 1951, see <ref
                        target="frus1951v06p1#pg_132">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, Part
                        1, pp. 132</ref> ff. For the text of the treaty, see 3 UST (pt. 3) 3947.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
